SUMMARY:🌳☀️ HIGH PARK SUNDAY WALK & PICNIC ☀️🌳
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌳☀️ HIGH PARK SUNDAY WALK
  & PICNIC ☀️🌳\n\n**Toronto's Biggest Park\, Hidden Trails\, The Zoo
  & A Relaxing Sunday Afternoon**\n\nThere are few better ways to spend a S
 unday than wandering through High Park with good people\, great conversati
 on\, and no real rush to be anywhere.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed afternoon e
 xploring Toronto's largest and most beloved park. High Park has a little b
 it of everything—peaceful forest trails\, beautiful gardens\, Grenadier 
 Pond\, wildlife\, open green spaces\, and even its own free zoo. It's one 
 of those places where you can forget you're in Canada's largest city.\n\nT
 his isn't about racing from one landmark to another.\nIt's about slowing d
 own\, getting outside\, meeting new people\, and enjoying a few hours toge
 ther in one of Toronto's best parks.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[
  Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n
 ***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend approximately **3 hou
 rs** exploring many of High Park's most beautiful areas at a relaxed socia
 l pace.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n🌳 Wander through shaded forest trails\
 n🦆 Visit beautiful Grenadier Pond\n🦙 Stop by the famous High Park Zo
 o to visit the animals\n🌼 Explore some of the park's quieter hidden cor
 ners\n🧺 Take a relaxing **30-minute picnic break**\, giving everyone a 
 chance to sit\, eat\, chat\, and get to know one another\n\n😊 Enjoy one
  of Toronto's best Sunday afternoons together\n\nThis route avoids the lar
 ge staircase found on some of our other High Park walks\, making it a litt
 le more relaxed. There are still a few gentle hills throughout the park\, 
 but nothing overly challenging for most walkers.\nThe goal isn't simply to
  walk through High Park.\nThe goal is to create enough time together that 
 conversations can happen naturally and new friendships have a chance to be
 gin.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place r
 ain or shine.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and wear comfort
 able walking shoes.\nWe'll keep a relaxed\, steady pace with plenty of opp
 ortunities to enjoy the scenery and chat along the way.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 
 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** High Park Sign (west side of B
 loor Street & High Park Avenue)\n🫎 I'll be wearing my **Moose Hat**\n
 ⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Earl
 y is on time. On time is late.**\nWe'll leave promptly so everyone can enj
 oy the full walk together.\n\n🏁 **End Point:** Back at High Park Subway
  Station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-trans
 fer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com
 )**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing
  events like this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 
 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧺 Lun
 ch or snacks for our picnic break\n🥪 Something small to share with the 
 group if you'd like\n🧴 Sunscreen\n🕶️ Sunglasses\n🐿️ Your Sund
 ay afternoon spirit\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is op
 en to anyone who wants to get outside\, meet new people\, and make friends
 —whether you're single or not.\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks &
  hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere'
 s always something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're always welcom
 e to just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nAs alw
 ays\, sometimes plans change and events may need to be cancelled—please 
 keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** M
 athew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 **[torontomoviesan
 doutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**C
 ome for the park.**\n**Stay for the picnic.**\n\n**Leave with a few more n
 ames in your phone than when you arrived.** 🌳🧺✨
