SUMMARY:🌿 Hogg's Hollow Summer Evening Walk & Dinner 🌅
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n### 🌿 Hogg's Hollow Summer Even
 ing Walk & Dinner 🌅\n\nJoin us for a beautiful **summer evening walk** 
 through **Hogg's Hollow**\, one of Toronto's most charming and historic ne
 ighbourhoods tucked away in the heart of North York. With its winding road
 s\, forested trails\, picturesque bridges\, and peaceful ravines\, it's ha
 rd to believe you're still in the city.\n\nWe'll stroll through the valley
  where the **West Don River** winds its way past historic homes\, quiet st
 reets\, and lush green spaces. Along the way\, we'll explore the area's fa
 scinating history—from **James Hogg**\, the Scottish settler who establi
 shed a mill here in the 1820s\, to the tragic\n\n**Hogg's Hollow Disaster*
 * of 1960\, when five workers lost their lives during the construction of 
 a water tunnel\, an event that forever changed workplace safety laws in On
 tario.\n\nAs the evening sun filters through the trees\, it's the perfect 
 opportunity to enjoy great conversation\, meet new people\, and discover o
 ne of Toronto's hidden gems.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click h
 ere to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n
 📍 **Meetup Location:**\n\nI'll be waiting near the **Shell gas station*
 * (easy to spot!) wearing my famous **Moose Hat** 🦌\n🏁 **Ending Spot
 :**\nRight back where we started.\n🕡 **Meetup Time:**\n**6:30 PM** *(I'
 ll wait just 5 minutes.)*\n\n🍗 **Dinner After**\n\nAfter the walk\, we'
 ll head to **Swiss Chalet** for a relaxed dinner. Whether you're joining f
 or the famous rotisserie chicken\, a salad\, or just great conversation\, 
 it's the perfect way to end a summer evening.\n\n💵 **Meetup Fee:** **$5
 ** (cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:m
 athewmaclean@hotmail.com)**)\n\n🥾 **What to Bring:**\n\n* Water 💧\n*
  Comfortable walking shoes\n* Bug spray (optional)\n* A camera—you never
  know what you'll spot! 📸\n\n☀️ **Weather**\nThis event takes place
  rain or shine\, except in cases of severe weather.\nAs we always say:\n\n
 **There's no such thing as bad weather—only unsuitable clothing.**\n\n**
 *\n\n**REMEMBER:** Feel free to just show up! If you're unsure of your pla
 ns\, you're always welcome to decide on the day.\n\n👤 **Organized by Ma
 thew**\nFor questions\, post on the event wall or email:\n**[torontomovies
 andoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**
