SUMMARY:🌅🍂 Sunset Walk: Glen Stewart Ravine & The Beach Boardwalk
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌅🍂 Sunset Walk: Glen Stewa
 rt Ravine & The Beach Boardwalk\n\n### A Short Fall Walk\, Ice Cream & Sun
 set by the Lake\n\nLooking for an easy way to spend a fall evening?\nJoin 
 us for a relaxed **sunset walk through Glen Stewart Ravine**\, followed by
  ice cream and a stroll along the Beach Boardwalk as the sun goes down.\n\
 nWe’ll start at **Main Station** and make our way through the neighbourh
 ood toward Glen Stewart Ravine. After enjoying the ravine and the fall col
 ours\, we’ll stop at **Ed’s Real Scoop** for ice cream. 🍦\n\nThen w
 e'll head toward the lake and walk along the **Beach Boardwalk**\, taking 
 in the evening light\, the water\, and the changing colours of the season.
 \nWe'll finish at **Woodbine Beach**\, where we'll take a little time to e
 njoy the sunset before wrapping up.\n\nThis is a **short\, easy walk of ab
 out 90 minutes**. There’s no rushing and no trying to conquer a trail 
 — just a beautiful evening\, something sweet to eat\, and good people to
  enjoy it with.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLI
 CK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 
 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet outside **Main Station** and mak
 e our way toward Glen Stewart Ravine.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* 🍂 Walk
  through Glen Stewart Ravine\n* 🌳 Enjoy the fall colours\n* 🍦 Stop a
 t **Ed’s Real Scoop** for ice cream\n* 🌊 Head down toward the lake\n*
  🚶‍♂️ Walk along the Beach Boardwalk\n* 🌅 Enjoy the sunset at 
 Woodbine Beach\n\nThe entire walk is approximately **90 minutes**\, depend
 ing on the pace of the group.\nThis is a **social walk**\, so we'll take o
 ur time and enjoy the evening.\n\n***\n\n## 🌅 Sunset & Weather\n\nThis 
 walk is all about enjoying the transition from **afternoon into evening**.
 \nThe temperature can feel cooler near the lake\, especially after sunset\
 , so bring an extra layer.\nWe'll walk **rain or shine unless severe weath
 er makes the walk unsafe**.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Mee
 tup Location:** Outside **Main Subway Station**\n🫎 Look for me in my **
 Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5
  minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** *
 *Woodbine Beach**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person o
 r e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support
  the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.
 \n**Ice cream is not included in the Meetup fee.** 🍦\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 
 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 A light 
 jacket or sweater\n🍦 A few dollars for ice cream\n📱 Your phone or ca
 mera for sunset photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is 
 great for:\n\n* Anyone looking for an easy evening outing\n* People who en
 joy walking but don't want a long hike\n* Anyone who loves fall colours\n*
  Ice cream lovers 🍦\n* People who want to meet others in a relaxed sett
 ing\n* Anyone who wants to watch the sunset by the lake\n\nThe activity is
  the container. **The people you meet along the way are the real experienc
 e.**\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just 
 show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things
  happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an
  eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuest
 ions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hot
 mail.com**\n\n**Come for the walk.**\n**Stay for the ice cream.**\n**Watch
  the sunset with us.** 🌅🍦
