SUMMARY:🌈 Rainbow Tunnel Walk - Toronto’s Historical Landmark
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌈 Rainbow Tunnel Walk\n\n### 
 A Hidden Piece of Toronto History\, Friendship & the Moccasin Trail\n\nYou
  may have driven along the **Don Valley Parkway** hundreds of times withou
 t realizing there was a story waiting just above you.\nThe **Rainbow Tunne
 l** is one of those unusual pieces of Toronto that feels almost like a sec
 ret. Painted in 1971 by teenager **B.C. Johnson** after the death of his f
 riend Sigred in a car accident\, the colourful tunnel became a lasting tri
 bute to friendship and loss.\n\nMore than 50 years later\, the artwork is 
 still part of the landscape.\nJoin us for an easy social walk through the 
 **Moccasin Trail and surrounding ravine paths**\, with the Rainbow Tunnel 
 as our destination.\n\nWe'll take our time\, stop for photos\, enjoy the t
 rails\, and learn a little about the story behind one of Toronto's more un
 usual landmarks.\nThis isn't a difficult hike or a formal historical tour.
  It's simply a chance to get outside\, discover something you may have dri
 ven past hundreds of times\, and spend a few hours with good people.\n\n
 📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://ch
 at.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What 
 We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet near **Don Mills & Lawrence** and begin walking eas
 t along Lawrence before connecting with the **Moccasin Trail**.\nAlong the
  way we'll:\n\n* Walk through the surrounding ravine and green spaces 🌳
 \n* Follow the Moccasin Trail\n* Visit the **Rainbow Tunnel** 🌈\n* Stop
  for photos and learn the story behind it\n* Continue along the surroundin
 g paths\n* Make our way back to where we started\n\nThe walk is approximat
 ely **2 hours**\, depending on the pace of the group.\nWe'll take our time
  rather than rushing through the route.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expe
 ctations\n\nThis walk takes place outdoors in typical Toronto weather.\nPl
 ease dress appropriately for the conditions and wear comfortable walking s
 hoes.\nThe route includes some **unpaved and uneven trail surfaces**\, so 
 good footwear is recommended.\nThis is a social walk\, not a race. We'll k
 eep a steady pace and take time to enjoy the surroundings.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of the **Royal B
 ank at Don Mills & Lawrence**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ 
 **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Ear
 ly is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Back at the Royal B
 ank\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**
 \n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and
  allows us to continue organizing walks and other events throughout Toront
 o.\n\n***\n\n## 🍰 After the Walk\n\nAfter returning to the starting poi
 nt\, anyone who wants to continue the afternoon can join us for a **social
  stop at Danish Pastry House**.\nCome for the walk. Stay for coffee\, past
 ries\, and conversation. ☕🥐\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 W
 ater\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥 Weather-appropria
 te clothing\n📱 Your phone or camera for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is
  This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy discovering hi
 dden parts of Toronto\n* Anyone interested in local history and unusual st
 ories\n* People who enjoy easy social walks\n* Anyone looking to meet new 
 people\n* People who simply want to spend a few hours outside\n\nThe Rainb
 ow Tunnel may be the destination\, but **the people you meet along the way
  are the real experience.**\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP
  ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your sche
 dule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or chan
 ged\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organ
 izer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **toront
 omoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the Rainbow Tunnel.**\n**Sta
 y for the friendship.**\n**Leave with a little more Toronto history — an
 d maybe a new connection.** 🌈💛
